# Accessibility (PinIt)

Apply these when adding or changing UI.

## Controls
- Icon-only buttons need an `aria-label` (e.g. "Add note", "Logout").
- Decorative icons: `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Do not rely on hover tooltips as the only accessible name. Tooltips must also show on `:focus-within`.

## Forms
- Every input needs a real `<label for>` or `aria-label` — never placeholder-only, never a fake `label="..."` attribute.
- Wire errors with `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, and `role="alert"`.
- On validation failure, move focus to the invalid field or the alert.

## Dialogs & disclosures
- Modals: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, `aria-labelledby`, `inert`/`aria-hidden` when closed, Escape closes, return focus to the trigger.
- Use `<h2>` (not `<h1>`) for dialog titles.
- Menus/toggles: `aria-expanded`, correct `aria-controls`, Escape closes, manage focus on open/close.

## Focus
- Keep visible `:focus-visible` outlines (do not remove with `outline: none` unless replaced).
- After opening add/edit UI, focus the first field — defer until after layout/async init (e.g. Editor.js `autofocus: false`, then focus).
- Do not leave a control "visually focused" but non-editable.

## Feedback & motion
- Flash/status messages: `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"` (or `#a11y-status` for async failures).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for open/close and transitions.
- Prefer text + color for errors; don't use color alone.

## Landmarks
- One skip link to `#main-content`.
- Label multiple `<nav>`s (`aria-label`).
- Page has a single primary `<h1>`; keep `lang` on `<html>`.
